  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \n\nA cold front will push through the area Wednesday night into \nThursday, bringing widespread precipitation. Some models are \nshowing a few areas getting over an inch, but most of the \nregion should receive lower amounts. There is a 10% chance that\nsome areas in southeast Ohio, northeast Kentucky, and western\nWest Virginia could get 2 inches. Models continue to struggle \nwith precipitation amounts however, so confidence is low. \nDespite some decent shear and low level helicity values, small \nCAPE values should prevent strong storms, although a rumble of \nthunder is possible.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nMuch cooler air will move in behind the cold front for the \nweekend. As high pressure builds in later in the weekend and\ninto the next work week, nighttime temperatures are expected to\nget cold enough for frost and freezing temperatures.",
